abuse expert, Dr. Emma Katz, said, This attempt to besmirch Caroline's character and make people think badly of her is of course an attempt to get Babas more sympathy and more lenient treatment, which goes completely against the narrative that he has any remorse or contrition for what he's done. In reference to Babas painting Caroline out to be the aggressor, Dr. Katz explained. We do often see victims argue. arguing back, and we see victims even physically fighting back against the coercive control. Sometimes people then think they can't be a real victim, they fought back.

